## PART 5 — FIX: MAHI MUST SEE THE SCREEN, CLICK, TYPE AND SWIPE (HIGH PRIORITY)

Audit result of the current code (verify, then fix):
- `MahiAccessibilityService.captureCurrentScreen()` already reads the screen into `ScreenSnapshot`, but Gemini Live NEVER receives it. `GeminiLiveClient` declares no function that reads the screen, so Mahi cannot "see" it.
- There is NO text typing anywhere (no `ACTION_SET_TEXT`), so Mahi cannot type.
- Tapping works only by matching text (`performActionOnMatchingNode`). There is no tap by element number, content description, view id or coordinates.
- `ScreenSnapshot.readableSummary` returns only 20 labels, too little to act on.
- `sendToolResponse(callId, name, resultMessage, success)` already exists, so tool results CAN be returned to Gemini. Use it.

Implement for real (add to `GeminiLiveClient` function declarations, `MahiTools`, `MahiAiEngine` tool list, `VoiceCommandRouter`):
1. **`readScreen`** tool: returns the current app package plus a numbered list of visible elements (index, label, type, clickable/editable/scrollable, bounds center). Cap about 60 elements, prioritise visible and actionable ones, skip password fields. The result goes back via `sendToolResponse` so Mahi can describe the screen and decide the next action. Refresh the snapshot each call (`rootInActiveWindow` can be null, retry briefly and handle it).
2. **`tapElement`** tool: tap by index (from the last `readScreen`), or by text / content description / view id, or by x,y. Prefer `ACTION_CLICK` on the node or a clickable parent, then fall back to `dispatchGesture` at the node center. After tapping, re-read the screen and report the result.
3. **`typeText`** tool: focus the target editable field (by index or the currently focused field) and set text with `ACTION_SET_TEXT`, with a clipboard `ACTION_PASTE` fallback. Support append vs replace, clear field, and pressing the keyboard action (search/send/enter) via `ACTION_IME_ENTER` (API 30+) or by tapping the on-screen button. Never type into password fields, and ask confirmation before sending messages, payments or other sensitive actions (reuse the existing confirmation flow).
4. **`swipe` / `scroll`**: keep the existing `screenGesture` tool, but also accept swipe by coordinates and by direction on a chosen element, and report success or failure back to Gemini.
5. **Visual fallback**: add `captureScreenImage` using `AccessibilityService.takeScreenshot()` (API 30+, needs `canTakeScreenshot="true"` in `mahi_accessibility_config.xml`). Send a downscaled JPEG to Gemini Live as `realtimeInput` image only when the user asks "screen dekho" and only when the accessibility node tree is empty or useless (games, Flutter, WebView, canvas apps). Nothing is captured in the background.
6. **Agent loop**: for requests like "YouTube kholo aur Mahi AI search karo", let Mahi chain steps: open app, `readScreen`, `tapElement`, `typeText`, press search, `readScreen` to verify. Stop after a step limit or when the same screen repeats, say what happened, and keep the existing `stopAutomation` working at all times.
7. **Service health**: if the accessibility service is off, the tool must say so clearly by voice and open the accessibility settings page. Keep the service alive across app restarts, and show an "Accessibility ON/OFF" status in the new Smart Smartphone Control menu. Add `flagRequestFilterKeyEvents`/other flags only if needed, and keep `flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows` plus `flagIncludeNotImportantViews`.
8. **Privacy**: never log or send screen content that looks like passwords, OTPs or card numbers; mask them. The user sees a visible indicator whenever Mahi reads the screen.
9. **Update the system prompt** in `MahiAiEngine` and the Gemini Live setup so the model KNOWS it can see and control the screen with these tools, and must call `readScreen` before answering any "screen par kya hai" question instead of guessing.

Acceptance test: say "screen par kya hai" in Chrome and Mahi names the real page and buttons. Say "search box mein cricket score likho aur search karo" and the text is really typed and submitted. Say "neeche scroll karo" and "left swipe karo" and the screen moves.

